---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const fulfillmentColumns = [
	[
		{
			src: '/fulfillment/loop/image1.webp',
			alt: 'Team member planning fulfillment workflows',
			className: 'aspect-[4/3]',
		},
		{
			src: '/fulfillment/loop/image4.avif',
			alt: 'Warehouse team working at computers',
			className: 'aspect-[4/5]',
		},
		{
			src: '/fulfillment/loop/image7.avif',
			alt: 'Warehouse operator reviewing stock',
			className: 'aspect-[4/5]',
		},
		{
			src: '/fulfillment/loop/image10.avif',
			alt: 'Fulfillment warehouse activity',
			className: 'aspect-[4/3]',
		},
	],
	[
		{
			src: '/fulfillment/loop/image2.avif',
			alt: 'Operator using equipment in the warehouse',
			className: 'aspect-[4/5]',
		},
		{
			src: '/fulfillment/loop/image5.avif',
			alt: 'Workers coordinating inventory tasks',
			className: 'aspect-[4/3]',
		},
		{
			src: '/fulfillment/loop/image8.avif',
			alt: 'Picking and packing products',
			className: 'aspect-[4/5]',
		},
	],
	[
		{
			src: '/fulfillment/loop/image3.avif',
			alt: 'Boxes stacked for fulfillment',
			className: 'aspect-[4/5]',
		},
		{
			src: '/fulfillment/loop/image6.avif',
			alt: 'Fulfillment associate in warehouse',
			className: 'aspect-[4/3]',
		},
		{
			src: '/fulfillment/loop/image9.avif',
			alt: 'Inventory movement across fulfillment floor',
			className: 'aspect-[4/5]',
		},
	],
];

const columnDurations = ['26s', '30s', '34s'];

const workflowSections = [
	{
		id: 1,
		layout: 'feature',
		image: '/fulfillment/content/image1.avif',
		alt: 'Team member using an inventory control app',
		title: 'Give team members an easy to use & workflow driven inventory control app.',
		introOne:
			'For great inventory management to happen, the first step is to give your team an easy way to do data-entry, without actually doing data-entry.',
		introTwo:
			'By using a workflow driven system, data entry happens as team members work. This can greatly increases accuracy, and speeds up task completion.',
		callout: 'Workflows with industry best practices built in.',
		tabs: ['Receive', 'Store', 'Recount', 'Move'],
		items: [],
		cards: [],
		featureTitle: 'Receiving Products',
		featureBody:
			'This is not only the start of your inventory management journey, but this step is crucial to get right as having accurate inventory counts begins with this process.',
		quicktip:
			'If you can get incoming shipment information like expected arrival dates or quantities of products in advance receiving will be much faster.',
	},
	{
		id: 2,
		layout: 'grid',
		tabs: [],
		cards: [],
		items: [
			{
				title: 'Storing Inventory',
				paragraphs: [
					'Knowing where products are and how much you actually have is an important part of daily inventory & order fulfillment operations.',
					'Once your team has clarity when it comes to that, you can start really optimizing the process in terms of where to place products to speed up the rest of the processes in your fulfillment center.',
					'Common efficiency gains can come from what level of racking you place certain products on, how far away from inbound & outbound stations, and so much more.',
				],
			},
			{
				title: 'Moving Locations',
				paragraphs: [
					'The process of relocating products from one bin or location to another seems simple, and it can be as long as your team is religious about logging movement within the facility.',
					'The good news is that many inventory control systems like ours will track those movements as they are made through easy workflows in the mobile app or on the web application.',
					"Order fulfillment would be very hard if someone doesn't know where something is because the data is not accurate or updated.",
				],
			},
			{
				title: 'Counting & Recounting',
				paragraphs: [
					'Counting inventory or recounting inventory is an important maintenance task that helps to ensure inventory is accurate.',
					'Cycle counting or blind counting are common processes that can be used to keep everything up to date when done from time to time.',
				],
				quicktip:
					'The more your team utilizes the other workflows correctly, the less counting and recounting you will need to do.',
			},
			{
				title: 'Picking & Packing',
				paragraphs: [
					'This process is the backbone of your order fulfillment operations. If your team has utilized the other processes here well, this should be a highly efficient and error-free process.',
					'Order fulfillment metrics to pay attention to would be picking accuracy, inventory accuracy, order cycle time, picks per hour, etc..',
					'There are also many different picking styles and ways to organize them that can drive efficiency in your order fulfillment process.',
				],
			},
		],
	},
	{
		id: 3,
		layout: 'management',
		image: '/fulfillment/content/image2.avif',
		alt: 'Management team monitoring a fulfillment floor',
		title: 'Provide management with tools to monitor, organize, and optimize the work.',
		introOne:
			'Once your team has covered basic workflows, a great next step is to allow management to monitor, organize, and optimize inventory & order fulfillment operations for efficiency gains.',
		introTwo:
			'The key to turn managers into a strategic leadership layer for your inventory management operations is to make sure they have the data they need to make better decisions.',
		featureBody:
			'This could be done using dashboards, easily searchable data, reporting, and even with the help of AI.',
		items: [],
		tabs: [],
		cards: [
			{
				tone: 'light',
				title: 'Monitoring critical inventory management activities can be done quickly with a great KPI-driven dashboard.',
				stat: '31% of warehouses face workforce efficiency challenges',
				source: 'Cognitops',
			},
			{
				tone: 'dark',
				title: 'Organizing task importance by quickly filtering data allows you to keep your team focused on the most relevant tasks.',
				stat: '31% of warehouses face workforce efficiency challenges',
				source: 'Cognitops',
			},
			{
				tone: 'light',
				title: 'Optimize the whole fulfillment center by addressing bottlenecks, streamlining inventory allocation, and fostering continuous improvement.',
				stat: '31% of warehouses face workforce efficiency challenges',
				source: 'Cognitops',
			},
		],
	},
];

const marketplaceLogos = {
	shopify: '/logos/shopify.avif',
	amazon: '/logos/amazon.avif',
	tiktok: '/logos/tiktok.avif',
	ebay: '/logos/ebay.avif',
	walmart: '/logos/walmart.avif',
	etsy: '/logos/Etsy.avif',
	binlogic: '/logos/mainLogo.svg',
};
---

<Layout>
	<section class="px-6 pb-12 pt-24 md:px-10 md:pb-16 md:pt-30 xl:px-12 xl:pb-20 xl:pt-34">
		<div class="mx-auto grid max-w-350 gap-10 xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.05fr)_minmax(560px,0.95fr)] xl:items-center xl:gap-12">
			<div class="max-w-2xl xl:pl-6">
				<h1 class="text-2xl font-medium leading-[1.04] tracking-[-0.04em] text-[#080F46] sm:text-3xl lg:text-[1rem] xl:text-[3rem] 2xl:text-[3.3rem]">
					Build &amp; run a world-class order fulfillment operation.
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-8 max-w-xl text-lg font-normal leading-8 text-[#2C386A] sm:text-xl sm:leading-9">
					We've seen many organizations achieve inventory control and order fulfillment mastery, but a common factor always seems to be having a great plan.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
					<a
						href="#"
						class="inline-flex min-w-52 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0A67AA] px-8 py-4 text-lg font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-[#085892]"
					>
						Get Started
					</a>
					<a
						href="#"
						class="inline-flex min-w-52 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-[3px] border-[#080F46] px-8 py-4 text-lg font-semibold text-[#080F46] transition hover:bg-[#080F46] hover:text-white"
					>
						See Demo
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="fulfillment-mosaic relative overflow-hidden rounded-4xl xl:rounded-[2.4rem]">
				<div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 left-0 z-10 w-7 bg-linear-to-r from-[#F2F2F2] via-[#F2F2F2]/48 to-transparent sm:w-12"></div>
				<div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 right-0 z-10 w-7 bg-linear-to-l from-[#F2F2F2] via-[#F2F2F2]/48 to-transparent sm:w-12"></div>
				<div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-0 z-10 h-10 bg-linear-to-b from-[#F2F2F2] via-[#F2F2F2]/42 to-transparent sm:h-14"></div>
				<div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-10 h-10 bg-linear-to-t from-[#F2F2F2] via-[#F2F2F2]/42 to-transparent sm:h-14"></div>

				<div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 md:grid-cols-3 md:gap-5">
					{
						fulfillmentColumns.map((column, columnIndex) => (
							<div class:list={[
								"fulfillment-column relative h-136 overflow-hidden sm:h-168 lg:h-192",
								columnIndex === 2 && 'col-span-2 mx-auto max-w-[18rem] md:col-span-1 md:mx-0 md:max-w-none',
							]}>
								<div class="fulfillment-track flex flex-col gap-4 md:gap-5" style={`--loop-duration: ${columnDurations[columnIndex]};`}>
									{[...column, ...column].map((image, imageIndex) => (
										<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[1.4rem] bg-white shadow-[0_18px_40px_rgba(8,15,70,0.10)]" aria-hidden={imageIndex >= column.length ? 'true' : 'false'}>
											<img
												src={image.src}
												alt={imageIndex >= column.length ? '' : image.alt}
												loading={imageIndex < column.length ? 'eager' : 'lazy'}
												class:list={['h-full w-full object-cover', image.className]}
											/>
										</div>
									))}
								</div>
							</div>
						))
					}
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="px-0 pb-16 pt-8 md:pb-24 md:pt-12">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 md:px-10 xl:px-12">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl overflow-hidden rounded-4xl bg-[#F8FBFE] px-6 py-12 text-center md:px-10 md:py-16">
				<div
					class="rounded-3xl px-4 py-8 md:px-10 md:py-10"
					style="background-image: linear-gradient(to right, rgba(10,103,170,0.14) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(10,103,170,0.14) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 24px 24px; background-position: center;"
				>
					<h2 class="text-4xl font-medium leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.04em] text-[#080F46] sm:text-5xl lg:text-[3.8rem]">
						Fulfillment Center Blueprint.
					</h2>
					<p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg font-normal leading-8 text-[#213165] sm:text-xl sm:leading-9">
						Having an operational blueprint is essential to creating and running world-class fulfillment centers.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-10 md:mt-14">
			<div class="relative h-96 overflow-hidden md:h-112 lg:h-136">
				<img
					src="/fulfillment/intro.webp"
					alt="Warehouse team member working on inventory management planning"
					loading="lazy"
					class="h-full w-full scale-110 object-cover object-[58%_0%]"
				/>
				<div class="absolute inset-0 bg-linear-to-r from-[#070B1E]/72 via-[#070B1E]/58 to-[#070B1E]/46"></div>
				<div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center">
					<div class="max-w-4xl px-6 py-8 text-white md:px-10 md:py-10 lg:px-20">
						<h3 class="text-3xl font-light leading-[1.04] tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-4xl lg:text-[3.25rem]">
							Order fulfillment starts with building out great processes for <span class="font-semibold">inventory management.</span>
						</h3>
						<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-base font-light leading-7 text-white/95 sm:text-lg sm:leading-8">
							Create great system-driven processes to work with your inventory so your team is prepared to handle any inventory or order fulfillment situation.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="px-0 pb-18 pt-6 md:pb-24 md:pt-10">
		<div class="space-y-0">
			{
				workflowSections.map((section, index) => (
					<article
						class:list={[
							"sticky border-t-10 border-[#00032A] bg-[#F2F2F2]",
							index === 0 ? 'top-18' : index === 1 ? 'top-24 -mt-20' : 'top-30 -mt-20',
						]}
						style={`z-index: ${index + 1};`}
					>
						{section.layout === 'grid' ? (
							<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 md:px-10 md:py-20 xl:px-12">
								<div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-x-16 gap-y-14 lg:grid-cols-2">
									{
										section.items.map((item) => (
											<div class="text-left">
												<div class="flex items-start gap-5">
													<span class="mt-1 h-10 w-2 bg-[#0A67AA]"></span>
													<h3 class="text-xl font-medium leading-tight text-[#363A41] sm:text-2xl lg:text-[2rem]">
														{item.title}
													</h3>
												</div>
												<div class="mt-5 space-y-6 text-sm font-normal leading-6 text-[#5A5E67] sm:text-base sm:leading-7 lg:text-lg lg:leading-8">
													{item.paragraphs.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
													{
														item.quicktip && (
															<p>
																<span class="font-semibold text-[#30343C]">Quicktip</span>
																<span class="italic"> {item.quicktip}</span>
															</p>
														)
													}
												</div>
											</div>
										))
									}
								</div>
							</div>
						) : section.layout === 'management' ? (
							<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-14 md:px-10 md:py-18 xl:px-12">
								<div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,34rem)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:items-start lg:gap-18 xl:gap-24">
									<div class="flex flex-col gap-6 md:gap-8 lg:pr-4">
										{
											section.cards.map((card, cardIndex) => (
												<div
													class:list={[
														"w-full max-w-116 rounded-[1.75rem] px-6 py-6 shadow-[0_18px_36px_rgba(8,15,70,0.06)] md:px-8 md:py-7",
														card.tone === 'dark' ? 'self-end bg-[#040733] text-white lg:mr-2' : 'self-start bg-white text-[#1B2348]',
														cardIndex === 0 ? 'lg:ml-0' : '',
														cardIndex === 2 ? 'lg:ml-0' : '',
													]}
												>
													<p class="text-sm leading-6 sm:text-base sm:leading-7 lg:text-lg lg:leading-8">
														<span class={card.tone === 'dark' ? 'font-semibold text-white' : 'font-semibold text-[#121A44]'}>
															{card.title.split(' ')[0]}
														</span>{' '}
														{card.title.substring(card.title.indexOf(' ') + 1)}
													</p>
													<div class="mt-6 flex items-start gap-4">
														<span class="mt-1 h-7 w-1 bg-[#0A67AA]"></span>
														<div>
															<p class:list={[
																"text-sm leading-6 sm:text-base sm:leading-7",
																card.tone === 'dark' ? 'text-white/95' : 'text-[#4F5566]',
															]}>
																{card.stat}
															</p>
															<p class:list={[
																"mt-2 text-sm",
																card.tone === 'dark' ? 'text-white/90' : 'text-[#1B2348]',
															]}>
																{card.source}
															</p>
														</div>
													</div>
												</div>
											))
										}
									</div>

									<div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center lg:items-start lg:text-left">
										<h3 class="max-w-2xl text-xl font-medium leading-[1.14] tracking-[-0.03em] text-[#080F46] sm:text-2xl lg:text-[2rem]">
											{section.title}
										</h3>
										<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm font-normal leading-6 text-[#4A4F63] sm:text-base sm:leading-7 lg:text-lg lg:leading-8">
											{section.introOne}
										</p>
										<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm font-normal leading-6 text-[#4A4F63] sm:text-base sm:leading-7 lg:text-lg lg:leading-8">
											{section.introTwo}
										</p>
										<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm font-normal leading-6 text-[#4A4F63] sm:text-base sm:leading-7 lg:text-lg lg:leading-8">
											{section.featureBody}
										</p>

										<div class="mt-8 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-[1.8rem] bg-slate-200 shadow-[0_24px_48px_rgba(8,15,70,0.12)]">
											<img
												src={section.image}
												alt={section.alt}
												loading="lazy"
												class="aspect-[1.9/1] h-full w-full object-cover"
											/>
										</div>
									</div>
								</div>
							</div>
						) : (
							<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-14 md:px-10 md:py-18 xl:px-12">
								<div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(400px,0.95fr)] lg:items-start lg:gap-12 xl:gap-16">
									<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-2xl flex-col justify-center text-center lg:mx-0 lg:text-left">
										<h3 class="text-xl font-medium leading-[1.14] tracking-[-0.03em] text-[#080F46] sm:text-2xl lg:text-[2rem]">
											{section.title}
										</h3>
										<p class="mt-6 text-sm font-normal leading-6 text-[#4A4F63] sm:text-base sm:leading-7 lg:text-lg lg:leading-8">
											{section.introOne}
										</p>
										<p class="mt-6 text-sm font-normal leading-6 text-[#4A4F63] sm:text-base sm:leading-7 lg:text-lg lg:leading-8">
											{section.introTwo}
										</p>

										<div class="mt-10 rounded-4xl bg-white px-8 py-8 shadow-[0_20px_48px_rgba(8,15,70,0.08)]">
											<p class="max-w-xl text-xl font-light leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.03em] text-[#61656F] sm:text-2xl lg:text-[2rem]">
												{section.callout}
											</p>
											<div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-6 gap-y-4 lg:justify-start">
												{
													section.tabs.map((tab) => (
														<div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-[#10183F]">
															<span class="h-7 w-1 bg-[#0A67AA]"></span>
															<span class="text-base font-medium sm:text-lg">{tab}</span>
														</div>
													))
												}
											</div>
										</div>
									</div>

									<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-2xl flex-col items-center text-center lg:mx-0 lg:items-start lg:text-left">
										<div class="w-full overflow-hidden rounded-[1.8rem] bg-slate-200 shadow-[0_24px_48px_rgba(8,15,70,0.12)]">
											<img
												src={section.image}
												alt={section.alt}
												loading="lazy"
												class="aspect-[1.28/1] h-full w-full object-cover"
											/>
										</div>

										<div class="mt-10 w-full">
											<div class="flex items-start justify-center gap-4 lg:justify-start">
												<span class="mt-2 h-10 w-2 bg-[#0A67AA]"></span>
												<h4 class="text-xl font-medium leading-tight text-[#30343C] sm:text-2xl lg:text-[2rem]">
													{section.featureTitle}
												</h4>
											</div>
											<p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm font-normal leading-6 text-[#4A4F63] sm:text-base sm:leading-7 lg:text-lg lg:leading-8">
												{section.featureBody}
											</p>
											<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-[#4A4F63] sm:text-base sm:leading-7 lg:text-lg lg:leading-8">
												<span class="font-semibold text-[#30343C]">Quicktip</span>
												<span class="italic"> {section.quicktip}</span>
											</p>
										</div>
									</div>
								</div>
							</div>
						)}
					</article>
				))
			}
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="px-0 py-0">
		<div class="relative overflow-hidden border-b-12 border-[#00032A]">
			<img
				src="/fulfillment/content/image3.avif"
				alt="Warehouse worker connecting channels and order fulfillment operations"
				loading="lazy"
				class="h-128 w-full object-cover object-[76%_0%] md:h-152 lg:h-164"
			/>
			<div class="absolute inset-0 bg-linear-to-r from-[#090E29]/84 via-[#090E29]/62 to-[#090E29]/38"></div>
			<div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center">
				<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-6 md:px-10 xl:px-12">
					<div class="max-w-4xl text-white">
						<h3 class="max-w-3xl text-3xl font-light leading-[1.08] tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-4xl lg:text-[3rem]">
							<span class="font-semibold">Connecting channels</span> to your inventory &amp; order fulfillment team and vis versa.
						</h3>
						<p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-base font-light leading-7 text-white/95 sm:text-lg sm:leading-8">
							Integrate all the places where customers want to buy from you. Give those channels a path to see your inventory availability, send your team orders for order fulfillment, and updates to serve your customers.
						</p>
						<a
							href="#"
							class="mt-7 inline-flex min-w-72 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-white px-8 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-white hover:text-[#0A0F2B] sm:text-lg"
						>
							See all chanels.
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="px-6 py-16 md:px-10 md:py-22 xl:px-12">
		<div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.95fr)_minmax(0,1.05fr)] lg:items-start lg:gap-16">
			<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl">
				<h3 class="max-w-xl text-2xl font-medium leading-[1.14] tracking-[-0.03em] text-[#080F46] sm:text-3xl lg:text-[2.65rem]">
					Let your inventory management system talk to all your channels.
				</h3>

